# Python Port Plan — Step 08: The REPL Loop

## Goal

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/08_the_repl_loop` to
`week1_baseline/python/08_the_repl_loop`. This step adds a second top-level
entry point, `Boukensha.repl(...) do ... end`, that stays alive across many
turns instead of running once: it reads a task from stdin, runs the agent,
prints the reply, and loops — with conversation history accumulating across
turns via a shared `Context`. Built-in commands: `/quiet`, `/loud`,
`/clear`, `/help`, `/exit`/`/quit`. Also fixes a real cross-turn bug in
`Agent` (the final assistant reply was never added to `Context.messages`,
which didn't matter for one-shot `run()` but breaks REPL history), adds a
3-tier config directory resolution (explicit env var → `./​.boukensha` in
the CWD → `~/.boukensha`), a friendlier 401 error message in `Client`, and a
`VERSION` constant.

**⚠️ Same safety profile as steps 5–7, but now genuinely open-ended.**
`example.py` starts an interactive REPL against the live Anthropic API —
unlike every prior step's fixed single task, a human at the keyboard can
drive arbitrarily many real API calls. Treat running this the same way as
prior live-API steps: confirm before actually starting an interactive
session during testing.

